    kind: "text",
    body: "every year me and friends go to Newport folk festival. There are three stages and it’s hard to prioritize who to see and how to navigate conflicts.\n\nI want to create a mobile friendly web app for all of us to use.\n\nCore features I’m thinking (open to suggestions or additions):\n1. schedule with the ability to sort alphabetically, by stage, or by time each day\n2. Something beyond hearting or favoriting: stack rank each day.\n3. Able to see how friends ranked\n4. Intelligent optimization of “your schedule” which makes it easy to get to at least some of what I’ve prioritized. This should factor time it takes to get between stages and where I’m coming from and going next in terms of sets\n5. link to Spotify for each artist along with expected festival metadata\n\nI’m building this through a narrow use case for now but would also love to consider selling this to festivals as a white label app. Keep that in mind but it is not v1. V1 is for us",
