    id: "2026-02-10-harissa-chicken-bowl",
    date: "2026-02-10",
    time: "1:37pm",
    kind: "text",
    body: "Harissa Chicken Bowl by me (and Claude)\n\n**For the chicken:**\nMarinate chicken thighs (more forgiving than breasts) in harissa, olive oil, lemon juice, minced garlic, and a touch of honey for at least 30 minutes. Grill or pan-sear until charred and cooked through, then slice.\n\n**Bowl base:**\nStart with something neutral like couscous, quinoa, or rice. Couscous is traditional and cooks in 5 minutes, or you could do herbed rice with parsley and lemon zest.\n\n**Toppings that balance the heat:**\n\n- Cucumber and tomato salad with red onion\n- Pickled red onions or quick-pickled vegetables\n- Chickpeas (roasted or just rinsed and seasoned)\n- Feta or goat cheese crumbles\n- Fresh herbs - cilantro, parsley, or mint\n- Harissa yogurt sauce (heavy on the yogurt, light on the harissa)\n\n**Something green:**\nArugula or mixed greens dressed simply with lemon and olive oil, or roasted broccoli/zucchini if you want something cooked.\n\nThe contrast between the warm spiced chicken, cool yogurt sauce, tangy pickles, and fresh vegetables really makes it work. You can meal prep the chicken and grain ahead, then assemble fresh each day.",
